  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SOCIAL SUPPORT FOR RESILIENT  LIVELIHOODS PROJECT(SSRLP). SOCIAL PROTECTION MULTIDONOR TRUST FUND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Irelands funding covers 25,000 housholds with this project. The project is intended to directly support ultra-poor  and labour constrained households to reduce poverty and stimulate  overall economic activity  in the rural districts .  The programme ensures women are included in the design of the programmes so that the programme meets their specific needs.   The programme often provides targeted benefits to women such  as direct cash transfers to female headed households recognising their vulnerability.  The programme also provides income generating activities and skills training specifically for women and encourages them to join micro finance and savings groups.  By providing the cash transfers, beneficiries are able to adapt to effects of climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
